{
  "name": "117. Routing custom provider fallback loaded at boot (#7538)",
  "description": "Pins #7538: a routing rule's legacy 'provider/model' fallback naming a custom provider must survive a restart. Rules are decoded from the config store and config.json before bifrost.Init registers custom providers, so since the fallback key-pin change (#7379) the prefix was not recognised at decode time, the fallback was frozen with an empty provider, and the routing plugin skipped it: the primary's error went straight back to the client while GET /api/routing/rules still listed the fallback. The static rule harness-custom-provider-fallback-boot in tests/integrations/python/config.json (behind x-harness-custom-fallback: boot) targets OpenAI on a model OpenAI rejects and falls back to 'openai_pc_auto/gpt-4o-mini'. Because the rule is loaded at boot, every run exercises the restart path without restarting. Pre-fix the request fails with the OpenAI primary's error; post-fix the custom provider serves it as fallback 1. The provider-only case pins the same boot path for the legacy 'openai_pc_auto/' form, which must take the incoming model. The API cases pin the rest of the fallback contract live: a pinned custom provider fallback created through the routing API skips a missing key and serves on its pinned key (the served key name is checked), the API round-trips standard and custom fallbacks in both forms through create, GET and PUT, and invalid fallbacks are rejected with 400. Every temporary rule is deleted by the case that created it.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "openai gpt-4o-mini custom provider fallback after boot non-streaming - #7538",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('boot-loaded custom provider fallback serves the request', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.equal(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-routing-info-is-fallback'), 'is-fallback header: ' + pm.response.text()).to.equal('true');",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-fallback-index'), 'fallback-index header: ' + pm.response.text()).to.equal('1');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('served by the custom provider named in the legacy fallback string', function () {",
              "  var json = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(json.extra_fields && json.extra_fields.provider, pm.response.text()).to.eql('openai_pc_auto');",
              "  pm.expect(json.choices).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-harness-custom-fallback",
            "value": "boot"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o-mini\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Reply OK.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"max_tokens\": 8,\n  \"stream\": false\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "chat",
            "completions"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
